Z||000003||frontal lobe||09-11-2000||06:18 PM||||Yeah, they sold all those stupid looking "dustbuster"-style minivans.  Worst part, now we will have to look at those stupid Azteks for the NEXT 15 YEARS on the road.||||reg||1
Z||000004||loafer87gt||09-11-2000||06:18 PM||||GM styling department should be shot in my opinion. I don't know what they are thinking, look at the Monte Carlo, the Grand Am is a nice car but the stupid side ridges totally ruin the car, and the TransAm has got so many damn scoops and buldges it is looks just plain tacky. Whereas other car companies seem to be trying to simplify and streamline the looks of their designs, GM just tries to add as much junk/scoops/ridges/crap to their old designs and release it to the public. The only GM car IMO that is very successful is the new Corvette. They managed to capture the character of the original car perfectly, and did it with a nice clean body design.||||reg||1
Z||000005||HugGRRRFiero||09-11-2000||06:32 PM||||I just love the Aztek, the countdown to picking up my Aztek was almost unbearable... I couldn't wait to drive it.  I bought the first one off the car hauler when it arrived at my local pontiac dealer.  It's been great and I like the fact that I can put my bike on the roof and go up north to go camping in the woods and it has the versatility to do anything and go anywhere.<P>The tent unfolds over the back real easy and takes no time to setup.  I feel like a kid all over again when I'm inside it.  Actually, I pumped up the inflatable air matress and slept in it in our driveway the first night I had it.  Sure beats the Holiday Inn!<P>I've had people give me blank looks while I'm driving around in it.  I figure they are just trying to think of all the reasons they should get one, they really should because they are missing out like big time.<P>What's especially great is you can take it to football games and have a tailgate party on back with pizza & rock tunes.  Radio volume controls are in the back too, so you don't even have to get up and adjust them from up front.  The speakers are even tilted rearward to give everyone in the party the ultimate outdoor stereo experience.<P>I know you guys all like the Fiero and stuff, but please give Pontiac a break, they have worked real hard to create this awesome looking sport activity vehicle.  I have high standards, and have no doubts the Aztek will live up to them.<P>I'm looking to buy another Aztek soon because of it's versatility, comfort, practicality, and edge features that make it so extremely innovative and fun.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||1
