Z||000009||rockcrawl||09-11-2000||08:27 PM||||Huggrrrrr, Sorry If I offended you with this post. I'm sure the Aztec has tons of great features. Sport utes are the <B>cool</B> thing to own right now (even though 90% of SUV owners don't need an SUV), so I bet they will sell. I just can't get over the looks of the thing. Why couldn't they just take the little blazer and add all the cool sporty features and give it a Pontiac makeover? If I wanted an SUV I'd be at the Ford dealer looking at the Sport-Trac. As for the rest of the Pontiac lineup, I don't think they look that bad. I like all the strakes and ridges combined with smooth curves (to a certain extent), and I especially like the current firebirds. <BR> loafer87gt, I agree with your opinion of the new Vette. It is the first Corvette that I have really liked, too bad I can't afford one!<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'86 GT 3800 (for sale)<BR>'87 GT (noisey 2.8)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)||||reg||10
Z||000010||HugGRRRFiero||09-11-2000||08:35 PM||||Ya guys, I'm ok, just woke up from in front of my computer...  man what a headache! <P>  I just seen what I had wrote, and don't remember a thing...  All I remember is bringing up the <A HREF="http://www.pontiac.com" TARGET=_blank>www.Pontiac.com</A> website, clicking on the Aztek section and started reading some of the adventures and experiences that people wrote in, that's the last thing I remember.  I guess Pontiac is giving people Azteks to use now and then letting them write about their experiences.  Boy, talk about some manufactured enthusiasm, it messed me up real bad...  everything is fine now.  Be careful if you check the site out...   no, no go and have some good laughs.<P>Hehe...  I was just kidding all along, hope I had you guys going for a minute.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">  <BR>  <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||12
